# Modules & starter themes

## Module / submodule standard

- Every feature is a **module** or **submodule** with a manifest (frontend `modules/*/manifest.ts`, backend module package).
- Register in the kernel registry (`frontend/src/kernel/registry.ts` + backend kernel). Enable/disable via activations — do not hard-wire routes that ignore activations.
- Admin page: `modules/{slug}/admin/{submodule}-page`.
- Public page: `modules/{slug}/site/{submodule}-page`.

```text
❌ BAD — dump a new page under src/views with no module/activation
✅ GOOD — manifest route + activation check + admin settings
```

## Starter themes

- Ship vertical UX as **`{vertical}-starter`** (e.g. `cafe-starter`, `ecommerce-starter` / shop starter).
- Theme folder: `frontend/src/themes/{slug}/` with `SiteHeader`, `SiteFooter`, views, `manifest.ts`.
- Register theme loaders in `theme-loader.ts`. Prefer starter as the default for new site types.

## Shared vs vertical

- **Shared (commerce):** payments, cart, checkout, catalog primitives, inventory hooks.
- **Vertical (cafe, magazine, …):** presentation, copy, extra fields — call shared APIs; do not fork payment gateways per vertical.

## Everything configurable

- Logo, favicon, accent, colors, fonts, nav labels, hero text, contact info → admin settings / branding API.
- Front-end reads branding from tenant/public API (`resolveSiteBranding`), never embeds fixed brand assets as the only option.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — fixed logo path with no settings
<img src="/brand/logo-fixed.png" />

// ✅ GOOD — from branding payload with fallback only for empty state
<SiteLogo logoUrl={branding.logo_url} siteName={siteName} />
```
